@ 8.5.2 - Proto-Turkic to Sakha
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Firespeaker.org wiki contributors (2014), “Turkic sound changes”. <http://wiki.firespeaker.org/Turkic_sound_changes>
	{e,ɤ}ː > je (the second one is conjectured based on my admittedly sparse knowledge of Turkish; I can only guess that 〈ė〉 is some sort of back unrounded vowel)
	o oɡ ø øɡ iɡ > wo ɥø o:[+ long] ø:[+ long] i:[+ long]
	a{ɡ̌(ɯ),b} {o{ɡ̌,b},aɡ̌u} u{ɡ̌,b} > ɰa wo u:[+ long]
	iɡ̌ > ɯ:[+ long]
	ɯ:[+ long] > i:[+ long]
	eɡ > {je,i:[+ long],ji}
	d s {ʃ,z} > t ∅ s / V_V
	s > ∅ / #_
	{z,ʃ} > h
	j > s (possibly only initially?)